# tally 2.3.1 R1, #248 face (a) (L §5.10, §8; E §4.2 step 5 "Each check is made only where the balance is
# known"): the sign rule isn't checked against a hole balance, and what reads past it is computed without it.
# Unchanged: a guard of the clause (the cut of L §5.10's own sentence).
=== hd_sign_q.tally
model hd_sign_q
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "probe"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place owed: claims PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place other: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input pd: date
input out_day: date
input pay: money PLN
input out: money PLN

move pay_in: transfers
  on pd
  leg cash from world to owed amount pay

move pay_out: transfers
  on out_day
  leg cash from owed to other amount out

ask o_apr5: bal(other, 2026-04-05)
ask o_flows: flows(other, 2026-04)
ask owed5: bal(owed, 2026-04-05)
ask p1: bal(other, 2026-04-05) with pd = 2026-04-01
ask p3: bal(other, 2026-04-05) with pd = 2026-04-03

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  opening[owed] = 50.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"
  opening[other] = 500.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"
  pd = ?"which day is the pay?" "s"
  out_day = 2026-04-02 "s"
  pay = 100.00 PLN "s"
  out = 80.00 PLN "s"
=== expect
o_apr5: 580.00 PLN
  cut 2026-01-01
o_flows: 80.00 PLN
  cut 2026-01-01
owed5: ?"which day is the pay?" (pd)
  cut 2026-01-01
p1: 580.00 PLN
  cut 2026-01-01
p3: refused: RUN-PLACE owed is -30.00 PLN after the day's observations and plans of 2026-04-02
  cut 2026-01-01
